le-server/results/run-20251113-152938\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"policy\\\": \\\"agent\\\",\\n      \\\"rate\\\": 140000,\\n      \\\"overall_latency_p99_avg_ms\\\": 17.216,\\n      \\\"overall_latency_p99_stddev_ms\\\": 0.0,\\n      \\\"overall_latency_p99_iterations_ms\\\": [\\n        17.216\\n      ],\\n      \\\"get_latency_p99_avg_ms\\\": 17.199,\\n      \\\"get_latency_p99_stddev_ms\\\": 0.0,\\n      \\\"get_latency_p99_iterations_ms\\\": [\\n        17.199\\n      ],\\n      \\\"scan_latency_p99_avg_ms\\\": 19.876,\\n      \\\"scan_latency_p99_stddev_ms\\\": 0.0,\\n      \\\"scan_latency_p99_iterations_ms\\\": [\\n        19.876\\n      ],\\n      \\\"run_dir\\\": \\\"/home/benny/evolve_agent/agentic-ebpf/pebble-server/results/run-20251113-152958\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\", \"perf_expl\": \"**Behavior & performance (precise)**  \\n- 50\\u202fk rps p99 collapsed to 2.34\\u202fms from the parent\\u2019s 509\\u202fms. The new selector injects per-packet randomness (`bpf_get_prandom_u32()` xor with the reuse hash, single slot pick) so GETs don\\u2019t keep hashing onto the same SCAN-heavy worker, letting queues drain before the 10\\u202f\\u00b5s synthetic GET service completes (`internal/server/config.go:36-38`, `internal/server/server.go:279-296`).  \\n- 60\\u202fk\\u2013100\\u202fk rps now stay in the 2.6\\u20134.6\\u202fms range versus 15\\u2013647\\u202fms before. Mixing randomness with constant-time slot selection keeps each worker\\u2019s backlog short, so even with 2\\u202fms SCAN busy-waits (`internal/server/config.go:39-41`, `internal/server/server.go:297-322`) the `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` pick rarely lands on a saturated socket, eliminating the multi-second queueing seen when deterministic hashes collided.  \\n- 140\\u202fk rps rose to 17.2\\u202fms (still a 380\\u00d7 improvement over the prior 6.6\\u202fs but notably worse than lower rates). Here every worker constantly runs 2\\u202fms scans, so even randomized selection often meets a full backlog; latency stays bounded but climbs because packets must wait for at least one SCAN to finish before the kernel admits them.  \\nConfidence: **High** (metrics directly show the gains and service times bound the theoretical minimums).\\n\\n**Did the behavior achieve the program\\u2019s intent? Why or why not?**  \\n- Intent: comments describe \\u201csingle-shot, randomized, division-free\\u201d steering to spread bursts while keeping verifier-friendly constant time.  \\n- Success: At \\u2264100\\u202fk rps the latency collapse relative to the parent run shows the randomized one-shot policy achieved its fairness/anti-hotspot goal\\u2014nearly uniform queueing allowed requests to complete close to their synthetic service limits.  \\n- Partial shortfall: At 140\\u202fk rps the policy cannot avoid congestion driven by SCAN service time; even though selection is randomized, it cannot conjure capacity once all workers\\u2019 busy-wait loops overlap, so intent is inherently unreachable at that load.\\n\\n**Missing signals & new metrics/logs to add**  \\n- Per-worker queue/backlog depth (what/why): log how many requests each worker has admitted but not yet replied to; reveals whether high-rate spikes are due to a few sockets or all of them saturating. (how): extend `workerStats` in `internal/server/server.go:328-360` to track in-flight counters, dumping them with the existing `[perf]` log lines.  \\n- `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` outcome counters (what/why): success/failure counts per packet would show whether the helper is regularly rejected (all target slots busy) or succeeding; clarifies when randomness really helps. (how): add a small percpu array map the userspace can read each second and reset, incrementing it in the selector around the helper call.\"}", "artifact_dir": "/home/benny/evolve_agent/agentic-ebpf/pebble-server/openevolve_output/db/artifacts/31d5c930-2ac1-41da-8ac5-efacdee14056", "embedding": null}, "parent_metrics": {"policy": "agent", "rates": [50000, 60000, 80000, 100000, 140000], "load_p99_curve": [[50000.0, 2.344], [60000.0, 2.622], [80000.0, 3.579], [100000.0, 4.637], [140000.0, 17.216]], "load_p99_stddev_curve": [[50000.0, 0.0], [60000.0, 0.0], [80000.0, 0.0], [100000.0, 0.0], [140000.0, 0.0]], "compile": 1.0, "load": 1.0, "combined_score": -60.606, "run_success": 1.0}, "parent_perf_expl": "**Behavior & performance (precise)**  \n- 50 k rps p99 collapsed to 2.34 ms from the parent’s 509 ms. The new selector injects per-packet randomness (`bpf_get_prandom_u32()` xor with the reuse hash, single slot pick) so GETs don’t keep hashing onto the same SCAN-heavy worker, letting queues drain before the 10 µs synthetic GET service completes (`internal/server/config.go:36-38`, `internal/server/server.go:279-296`).  \n- 60 k–100 k rps now stay in the 2.6–4.6 ms range versus 15–647 ms before. Mixing randomness with constant-time slot selection keeps each worker’s backlog short, so even with 2 ms SCAN busy-waits (`internal/server/config.go:39-41`, `internal/server/server.go:297-322`) the `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` pick rarely lands on a saturated socket, eliminating the multi-second queueing seen when deterministic hashes collided.  \n- 140 k rps rose to 17.2 ms (still a 380× improvement over the prior 6.6 s but notably worse than lower rates). Here every worker constantly runs 2 ms scans, so even randomized selection often meets a full backlog; latency stays bounded but climbs because packets must wait for at least one SCAN to finish before the kernel admits them.  \nConfidence: **High** (metrics directly show the gains and service times bound the theoretical minimums).\n\n**Did the behavior achieve the program’s intent? Why or why not?**  \n- Intent: comments describe “single-shot, randomized, division-free” steering to spread bursts while keeping verifier-friendly constant time.  \n- Success: At ≤100 k rps the latency collapse relative to the parent run shows the randomized one-shot policy achieved its fairness/anti-hotspot goal—nearly uniform queueing allowed requests to complete close to their synthetic service limits.  \n- Partial shortfall: At 140 k rps the policy cannot avoid congestion driven by SCAN service time; even though selection is randomized, it cannot conjure capacity once all workers’ busy-wait loops overlap, so intent is inherently unreachable at that load.\n\n**Missing signals & new metrics/logs to add**  \n- Per-worker queue/backlog depth (what/why): log how many requests each worker has admitted but not yet replied to; reveals whether high-rate spikes are due to a few sockets or all of them saturating. (how): extend `workerStats` in `internal/server/server.go:328-360` to track in-flight counters, dumping them with the existing `[perf]` log lines.  \n- `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` outcome counters (what/why): success/failure counts per packet would show whether the helper is regularly rejected (all target slots busy) or succeeding; clarifies when randomness really helps. (how): add a small percpu array map the userspace can read each second and reset, incrementing it in the selector around the helper call.", "code_summary": "{\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Synthetic UDP storage emulator with eBPF-aware load balancing (pebble-server) — only internal/, cmd/, scripts/, workload/, run.sh, run_exp.py included.\",\n    \"languages\": [\n      \"Go 1.22 (internal/*, cmd/*)\",\n      \"Bash (run.sh, scripts/*, workload/run_client.sh)\",\n      \"Python 3 (run_exp.py, scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py)\"\n    ],\n    \"artifact_conventions\": {\n      \"logs\": \"logs/<role> (server|client)\",\n      \"results\": \"results/run-* (per run.sh invocation) containing experiment.json + workload_summary.json\",\n      \"eBPF_pin_paths\": \"/sys/fs/bpf/pebble/<RUN_ID> (set by run.sh before launching the Go server)\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"execution_flow\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"Experiment orchestration\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run_exp.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Thin experiment wrapper: either shells into run.sh for fresh sweeps or parses dispatch manifests to summarise existing runs, then emits summary.json and optional matplotlib plots.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"parse_args (run_exp.py:29-95) exposes policies/rates/threads plus manifest + plotting toggles.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh/load_manifest_runs gather `run-*` directories, extract metrics from workload_summary.json, and pass records into write_experiment_summary/generate_plots.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"Per-run workflow\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run.sh\",\n      \"description\": \"Convenience script that (a) slices NUMA CPUs between server/client, (b) rebuilds eBPF assets, (c) restarts the Go server for each workload iteration, (d) runs cmd/workload_client under taskset, and (e) aggregates iteration outputs into workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool/join_by (run.sh:27-118) derive SERVER_CPUSET + CLIENT_CPUSET from CPUSET_POOL or NUMA node 0.\",\n        \"Calls scripts/build_ebpf.sh + scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh, then orchestrates server via scripts/launch_server.sh and client via run_client wrapper.\",\n        \"Embedded Python (run.sh:415-452) regex-parses client logs into workload_summary.json; final line prints the run directory for downstream tooling.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"Runtime services\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-91 -> internal/server/*\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-450\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Go binaries that run.sh controls. The server exposes UDP reuseport workers with synthetic latency and optional eBPF selection, while the workload client generates GET/SCAN traffic with latency tracking.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server wires CLI flags, creates log/results dirs, enables pprof/profiling, builds server.Config and runs server.New/Run under signal-aware context.\",\n        \"internal/server.Server.New/Run (server.go:104-181) validate config, load eBPF policy, clear pinned maps, then open reuseport sockets, attach eBPF, and spawn workers; handleRequest (server.go:268-325) executes busy-wait delays and records stats.\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client main loop (main.go:67-347) builds UDP payloads, enforces rate limit via golang.org/x/time/rate, tags each request with reqID (makeReqID/parseReqID, main.go:308-337) so receive goroutines can compute latency and feed the aggregator (latencyAggregator, main.go:40-66).\",\n        \"Server stats logger (server.go:328-395) emits per-worker and aggregate lines that scripts/monitoring can scrape.\"\n      ],\n      \"downstream\": [\n        \"Server relies on internal/server/ebpf.go + generated internal/ebpfutil bindings.\",\n        \"Client output is parsed by run.sh’s Python aggregator; logs feed human debugging.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"name\": \"Support scripts\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"scripts/build_ebpf.sh:1-34\",\n        \"scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh:1-25\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh:1-96\",\n        \"scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py:1-654\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh:1-62\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Reusable helpers for building eBPF assets, cleaning pinned maps, launching the server standalone, dispatching dockerized experiments, and invoking the workload client without run.sh.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"build_ebpf.sh enforces clang availability, sets BPF_CLANG/BPF_CFLAGS, adds arch include paths, then runs `go generate ./internal/ebpfutil`.\",\n        \"cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh deletes global pinned maps unless run-specific BPF_PIN_PATH is set, preventing fd leaks between runs.\",\n        \"launch_server.sh builds cmd/pebble_server (unless disabled), enforces single instance via PID file, applies taskset when SERVER_CPUSET is exported, and records PID for run.sh.\",\n        \"dispatch_docker_experiments.py reads NUMA topology (read_numa_cpu_map, line 106), assigns per-container CPU slices, constructs docker run commands (build_jobs, line 149), streams logs asynchronously (run_job, line 221), and optionally post-processes with run_exp.py.\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh is a thin CLI around `go run ./cmd/workload_client` for ad-hoc manual traffic.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"modules\": {\n    \"run_exp.py\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Top-level wrapper to sweep policies/rates and collect workload_summary.json files into one experiment summary.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"parse_args exposes knobs for policies/rates, send-workers, duration, server/client cores, plotting, and manifest reuse.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh executes run.sh and captures the run directory; load_manifest_runs + link_run_directories reuse docker-dispatched runs.\",\n        \"generate_overall_plot / generate_get_scan_plot optionally render PNGs (skip with --skip-plot).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"run.sh\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Automation glue that sets up CPU pinning, rebuilds eBPF assets, runs cmd/pebble_server + cmd/workload_client for N iterations, and emits workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool + join_by compute SERVER_CPUSET/CLIENT_CPUSET and export them for both taskset prefixes.\",\n        \"start_server/stop_server wrap scripts/launch_server.sh and enforce clean PID files; run_client pins workload_client under CLIENT_CPUSET.\",\n        \"Embedded Python generates workload_summary.json from logs/workload_iteration_*.txt, which run_exp.py later ingests.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/pebble_server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Go binary that instantiates internal/server.Server based on CLI flags and keeps it running with profiling enabled.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Flag wiring & filesystem setup\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-52\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Defines flags for listen addr, workers, policy, max scan, log/results dirs, timeouts, and synthetic delays; ensures directories exist before logging.\",\n            \"Creates/opens <log-dir>/server.log (append mode) and builds a microsecond-resolution logger.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Profiling + server lifecycle\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:52-92\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Enables block/mutex profiling (runtime.SetBlockProfileRate/SetMutexProfileFraction) and hosts net/http/pprof on 127.0.0.1:6060.\",\n            \"Builds server.Config, calls server.New (fails fast on invalid config or eBPF load issues), installs SIGINT/SIGTERM handler, logs startup configuration, and blocks on srv.Run(ctx).\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"Uses internal/server (Config, Server, eBPF loader).\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh expects -log-dir and -results-dir to exist for log collation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/workload_client\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Open-loop UDP workload generator with reqID-based latency measurement and throughput reporting.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Latency data structures\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:32-66\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"latencyRecord and latencyAggregator store per-request latencies, split into overall/GET/SCAN slices; aggregator.totalRecv reports sample counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Main workload loop\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-307\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Parses flags (server, duration, rate, get-frac, scan-limit, key prefix/space, log path, send workers), validates arguments, seeds RNGs per worker.\",\n            \"Creates a shared rate limiter (golang.org/x/time/rate), spawns send goroutines that build payloads (buildPayload, line 363) and assign reqIDs (makeReqID, line 308).\",\n            \"Spawns recv goroutines with deadlines that parse responses, extract reqIDs (parseReqID, line 320), compute latency, and push records into latencyCh.\",\n            \"Aggregator + monitor goroutines track outstanding requests and total received counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Statistics reporting\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:308-451\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Helper functions (makeReqID/parseReqID/writeHex/parseHex) ensure both sides share the encoding.\",\n            \"percentile/average/reportLatencyStats (lines 376-451) sort copies of the latency slices, compute p50/p90/p99/avg, and print textual summaries that run.sh’s regex parser expects.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"run.sh’s run_client wrapper invokes this with -log pointing at logs/client.log; workload/run_client.sh uses go run for convenience.\",\n        \"Server assumes GET payload format 'GET key [reqID]' and SCAN 'SCAN start limit [reqID]' as implemented here.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"internal/server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Core server runtime, including configuration validation, UDP worker pool, request parser, stats logging, and eBPF policy integration.\",\n      \"key_files\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/config.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Config struct + Validate clamp runtime knobs to sane defaults so CLI/script errors don’t crash the server.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Config.Validate\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/config.go:19-43\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Sets ListenAddr default (127.0.0.1:9000), ensures at least one worker, caps MaxScanKeys >= 1 (default 100k), enforces non-zero timeouts/delays.\",\n                \"Called by server.New before any socket/eBPF work, giving run.sh freedom to pass zero/negative placeholder values.\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/server.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Implements the Server struct, worker lifecycle, UDP handler, and stats reporter.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.New\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:104-131\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Validates config, builds default logger when nil, loads eBPF policy via loadEBPF, clears pinned target map when a program is present, and preallocates workerStats.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.Run\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:144-182\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Resets stats, spawns stats logger, iterates workers to open UDP sockets (openWorker, lines 184-230), optionally attaches the eBPF program to worker 0, records socket fds into the pinned map, launches spawnWorker goroutines, and blocks until ctx cancellation.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"openWorker + spawnWorker\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:184-266\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"openWorker sets SO_REUSEADDR/SO_REUSEPORT via net.ListenConfig.Control and attaches the eBPF program once; returns both UDPConn and fd for map updates.\",\n                \"spawnWorker loops on ReadFromUDP, handles ctx cancellation/ErrClosed gracefully, and logs transient read/write errors.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"handleRequest\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:268-325\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Parses payloads via parseRequest, extracts optional reqID tokens, enforces S